# Skills Vector design system

Locked visual world: **Evidence Atlas · Control** ("The Evidence Desk").

## Source of truth

- Read and follow `DESIGN.md` before any UI, mockup, or frontend change.
- Tokens live in `design-concepts/design-system/tokens.css`.
- Shared primitives live in `design-concepts/design-system/components.css`.
- Canonical product surface: `design-concepts/app.html`.

## Required

- Use semantic colors: `--present` (cobalt), `--uncertain` (clay), `--disagree` (wine). Never teal/cyan scrub greens or amber/yellow clinical warning pairs.
- Square corners (`border-radius: 0` unless DESIGN.md is explicitly revised).
- No thick colored left/right side-tab accents on cards, callouts, or claim lists — use top hairline (≤2px), full border, or wash.
- Type: STIX Two Text (findings/display), IBM Plex Sans (UI), IBM Plex Mono (data only).
- Evidence viz stay honest: presence / absence / disagreement — no fabricated coverage percentages.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Theme focus and `::selection` from present cobalt.

## Do not

- Do not revive Pixel Ops, Signal, Editorial Brutalism, or other archived explorations as product UI (`design-concepts/archive/` is historical only).
- Do not invent a second palette or rounded consumer-app chrome without an explicit redesign decision that updates DESIGN.md.
- Do not build UI that ignores DESIGN.md tokens.

When adding screens, match Control density, mineral wash atmosphere, instrument rail patterns, and callout/matrix language from `design-concepts/app.html`.
